 Old braun--

2378
01:27:01,630 --> 01:27:02,130
-Grrr.

2379
01:27:02,130 --> 01:27:02,690
-Hello.

2380
01:27:02,690 --> 01:27:04,290
-Hey, a m-monster.

2381
01:27:04,290 --> 01:27:05,810
-Who is clearly Mike.

2382
01:27:05,810 --> 01:27:07,420
-Gee, what happened, Mike?

2383
01:27:07,420 --> 01:27:10,650
-Oh, I got bit by a giant spider
 on my way in from the theater,

2384
01:27:10,650 --> 01:27:12,510
so now I'm a giant spider.

2385
01:27:12,510 --> 01:27:14,060
-Yeah, you're gonna see that.

2386
01:27:14,060 --> 01:27:15,380
Yeah, I gotta say,
 though, Mike, you

2387
01:27:15,380 --> 01:27:17,320
look even less like a
 spider than that guy

2388
01:27:17,320 --> 01:27:18,290
Gary did in the movie.

2389
01:27:18,290 --> 01:27:18,790
-Yeah.

2390
01:27:18,790 --> 01:27:19,090
Hm.

2391
01:27:19,090 --> 01:27:19,680
-Think so?

2392
01:27:19,680 --> 01:27:20,180
-Yeah.

2393
01:27:20,180 --> 01:27:25,990
-Yeah, you're still,
 like, 99.999999999% human.

2394
01:27:25,990 --> 01:27:27,100
-Mm, no.

2395
01:27:27,100 --> 01:27:28,530
I'm a, I'm a huge spider.

2396
01:27:28,530 --> 01:27:30,730
I, uh, I got this
 giant spider claw.

2397
01:27:30,730 --> 01:27:31,230
-Wow.

2398
01:27:31,230 --> 01:27:31,870
So, so what?

2399
01:27:31,870 --> 01:27:33,170
You're going to
 attack us with that

2400
01:27:33,170 --> 01:27:36,410
and drain out our
 essential life fluids, or?

2401
01:27:36,410 --> 01:27:37,110
-No, I--

2402
01:27:37,110 --> 01:27:37,610
-Oh?

2403
01:27:37,610 --> 01:27:40,040
-In fact I was going to make
 myself a braunschweiger melt.

2404
01:27:40,040 --> 01:27:41,430
-Now that's a coincidence!

2405
01:27:41,430 --> 01:27:42,820
[FORCED LAUGHTER]

2406
01:27:59,110 --> 01:28:00,070
-Well.

2407
01:28:00,070 --> 01:28:00,570
-Whoa.

2408
01:28:00,570 --> 01:28:01,210
[CLEARS THROAT]

2409
01:28:01,210 --> 01:28:01,710
-Hm.

2410
01:28:01,710 --> 01:28:02,990
[SIGH]

2411
01:28:02,990 --> 01:28:04,770
-Let's see what Pearl's up to.

2412
01:28:04,770 --> 01:28:07,010
-(WHISPERING) Yeah, let's.

2413
01:28:07,010 --> 01:28:08,210
MIKE (OFFSCREEN):
 The castle's gone.

2414
01:28:08,210 --> 01:28:13,450
There's nothing but a huge, dark
 stain from them blasting off.

2415
01:28:13,450 --> 01:28:14,060
-Ah, no, Mike.

2416
01:28:14,060 --> 01:28:17,320
The stain's from Bobo.

2417
01:28:17,320 --> 01:28:18,190
-Oh, sorry Nelson.

2418
01:28:18,190 --> 01:28:18,940
Forgot to tell you.

2419
01:28:18,940 --> 01:28:20,210
We're moving back.

2420
01:28:20,210 --> 01:28:23,500
They had some weird,
 arcane law in that town

2421
01:28:23,500 --> 01:28:26,000
about not throwing
 garbage out your windows.

2422
01:28:26,000 --> 01:28:29,220
And I cannot abide that
 kind of oppression.

2423
01:28:29,220 --> 01:28:32,590
So we got the castle back
 up on the flatbed out there.

2424
01:28:32,590 --> 01:28:35,330
We had to stop and diesel up
 at this here Pump-N-Munch.

2425
01:28:35,330 --> 01:28:36,160
Bobo's in the men's room.

2426
01:28:36,160 --> 01:28:38,020
Me and Brain Guy are
 here in the ladies' room.

2427
01:28:38,020 --> 01:28:39,930
-Oh, I had no idea.

2428
01:28:39,930 --> 01:28:40,920
-Right.

2429
01:28:40,920 --> 01:28:43,320
-Law-giver, Brain Guy, look.

2430
01:28:43,320 --> 01:28:45,890
I found a bunch of balloons in
 the men's room vending machine.

2431
01:28:45,890 --> 01:28:46,390
Ha!

2432
01:28:46,390 --> 01:28:47,770
So I bought us a whole bunch.

2433
01:28:47,770 --> 01:28:49,240
And look, they're
 individually wrapped!

2434
01:28:49,240 --> 01:28:52,000
Well, this one even
 protects us from something.

2435
01:28:52,000 --> 01:28:55,030
Oh, and this is from France,
 and it's supposed to tickle us.

2436
01:28:55,030 --> 01:28:56,460
-Ugh.

2437
01:28:56,460 --> 01:28:57,330
-That's fun.

2438
01:28:57,330 --> 01:28:58,630
Oh, and this one?

2439
01:28:58,630 --> 01:29:00,240
This is a ribbed
 balloons that's supposed

2440
01:29:00,240 --> 01:29:01,320
to make some lady happy.

2441
01:29:01,320 --> 01:29:02,280
I really don't understand--

2442
01:29:02,280 --> 01:29:03,590
-Can, can I see those, please?

2443
01:29:03,590 --> 01:29:04,510
-Oh, sure.

2444
01:29:04,510 --> 01:29:07,270
-Um, Bobo, we need to
 have, uh, a little talk.

2445
01:29:07,270 --> 01:29:08,040
-Huh?

2446
01:29:08,040 --> 01:29:10,390
-You're not ready
 for this, Nelson.

2447
01:29:10,390 --> 01:29:14,450
Now, Bobo, when a flower
 loves a bee very much--

2448
01:29:14,450 --> 01:29:14,950
-Oh.

2449
01:29:14,950 --> 01:29:15,450
Bobo.

2450
01:29:15,450 --> 01:29:17,260
[HUMMING]

2451
01:29:17,260 --> 01:29:23,230
-Oh, um, my many lady friends
 will appreciate my caution.

2452
01:29:23,230 --> 01:29:24,280
BOBO (OFFSCREEN): Oh.

2453
01:29:24,280 --> 01:29:26,380
[GIGGLING] Sweet.

2454
01:29:26,380 --> 01:29:27,280
[MUSIC PLAYING]

2455
01:29:35,980 --> 01:29:38,130
BOBO (OFFSCREEN):
 [MONKEY NOISES]

